{"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"ATProtoKit is designed to make it easy for you to interact with the AT Protocol and other services built on of the technology, such as Bluesky.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Creating-a-session","text":"Creating a session"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In order to log in, you need to create a session. To get started, create a new ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ATProtoKit\/documentation\/ATProtoKit\/ATProtocolConfiguration","isActive":true},{"text":" instance:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let config = ATProtocolConfiguration()"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Then, you can create a session with the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/ATProtoKit\/documentation\/ATProtoKit\/ATProtocolConfiguration\/authenticate(with:password:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" method:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["Task {","    try await config.authenticate(with: \"lucy.bsky.social\", password: \"hunter2\")","}"]},{"style":"important","type":"aside","name":"Important","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Do not use the password you typically use for signing into Bluesky: only use a specific App Password that’s in use for this instance of ATProtoKit only. To generate an App Password, go to the Bluesky website, then go to Settings > Privacy & Security > App Passwords and follow the instructions.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You can use a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"do-catch"},{"text":" block to create the ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ATProtoKit\/documentation\/ATProtoKit\/UserSession","isActive":true},{"text":" object (if the session was successfully created) or handle the error (if an error occured):","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let config = ATProtocolConfiguration()","","Task {","    do {","        try await config.authenticate(with: \"lucy.bsky.social\", password: \"hunter2\")","","        \/\/ Handle the success.","    } catch {","        \/\/ Handle the error.","    }","}"]},{"style":"note","type":"aside","name":"Note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you’ve enabled Two-Factor Authentication (via email), "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ATProtoKit\/documentation\/ATProtoKit\/ATProtocolConfiguration\/authenticate(with:password:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" waits for the code after the server returns "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AuthFactorTokenRequired"},{"type":"text","text":". Check your inbox for the code, then pass it to "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ATProtoKit\/documentation\/ATProtoKit\/AppPasswordAuthenticating\/receiveCodeFromUser(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" from your UI or command-line input handler."}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ATProtoKit\/documentation\/ATProtoKit\/UserSession","isActive":true},{"text":" will contain, among other things, the access and refresh tokens. ATProtoKit abstracts this away for you so you don’t need to add it every time you use a method that requires an active session.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You can then create an ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ATProtoKit\/documentation\/ATProtoKit\/ATProtoKit","isActive":true},{"text":" instance, where you can insert the ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ATProtoKit\/documentation\/ATProtoKit\/ATProtocolConfiguration","isActive":true},{"text":" object in the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sessionConfiguration"},{"text":" parameter:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["Task {","    let atProto = await ATProtoKit(sessionConfiguration: config)","}"]},{"level":3,"anchor":"Creating-a-post","type":"heading","text":"Creating a post"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"To create a post, first create an ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/ATProtoKit\/documentation\/ATProtoKit\/ATProtoBluesky","type":"reference"},{"text":" instance, with the ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ATProtoKit\/documentation\/ATProtoKit\/ATProtoKit","isActive":true},{"text":" instance as the parameter:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let atProtoBluesky = ATProtoBluesky(atProtoKitInstance: atProto)"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Then use the ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ATProtoKit\/documentation\/ATProtoKit\/ATProtoBluesky\/createPostRecord(text:inlineFacets:locales:replyTo:embed:labels:tags:creationDate:replyControls:embeddingRules:recordKey:shouldValidate:swapCommit:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" method. While this method is extremely extensive, we’re only going to focus on the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" parameter."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let postResult = try await atProtoBluesky.createPostRecord(text: \"Hello Bluesky!\")","print(postResult)"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You should see the post in your Bluesky account once you run this code. When the method successfully completes, you’ll receive a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/ATProtoKit\/documentation\/ATProtoKit\/ComAtprotoLexicon\/Repository\/StrongReference","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" object that contains the URI of the record ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ATProtoKit\/documentation\/ATProtoKit\/ComAtprotoLexicon\/Repository\/StrongReference\/recordURI","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") and the content identifier hash of the record ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ATProtoKit\/documentation\/ATProtoKit\/ComAtprotoLexicon\/Repository\/StrongReference\/recordCID","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"View Your Own Posts","anchor":"View-Your-Own-Posts"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To view your own posts, use"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ATProtoKit\/documentation\/ATProtoKit\/ATProtoKit\/getAuthorFeed(by:limit:cursor:postFilter:shouldIncludePins:labelersValue:)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and pass "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ATProtoKit\/documentation\/ATProtoKit\/UserSession\/handle"},{"type":"text","text":" as the first argument:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["do {","    guard let session = try await atProto.getUserSession() else { return }","    let myFeed = try await atProto.getAuthorFeed(by: session.handle)","    print(\"Feed: \\(myFeed)\")","} catch {","    throw error","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"By default, it will grab the first 50 posts from you, including replies, and without the pinned post. However, you can tweak that with the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"limit"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"postFilter"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"shouldIncludePins"},{"type":"text","text":" arguments. You can also poll more posts if a singular call reaches its limit by using "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ATProtoKit\/documentation\/ATProtoKit\/AppBskyLexicon\/Feed\/GetAuthorFeedOutput\/cursor"},{"type":"text","text":" with the next API call:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let myFeed = try await atProto.getAuthorFeed(","    by: \"lucy.bsky.social\",","    limit: 100",")","","print(\"Feed (first 100 posts): \\(myFeed)\")","","\/\/ To get the next 100 posts, call the method again,","\/\/ but attach the `cursor` as an argument.","","let myFeedExtended = try await atProto.getAuthorFeed(","    by: \"lucy.bsky.social\",","    limit: 100,","    cursor: myFeed.cursor",")","","print(\"Feed (next 100 posts): \\(myFeedExtended)\")"]}]}],"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ATProtoKit\/documentation\/ATProtoKit\/ATProtoKit","doc:\/\/ATProtoKit\/documentation\/ATProtoKit\/ATProtoAdmin","doc:\/\/ATProtoKit\/documentation\/ATProtoKit\/ATProtoBluesky","doc:\/\/ATProtoKit\/documentation\/ATProtoKit\/ATProtoBlueskyChat"],"title":"Essentials","anchor":"Essentials","generated":true}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/ATProtoKit\/documentation\/ATProtoKit\/Getting-Started-with-ATProtoKit","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/atprotokit\/getting-started-with-atprotokit"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Sign in with a Bluesky account, send a post, and view the account’s posts."}],"metadata":{"title":"Getting Started with ATProtoKit","modules":[{"name":"ATProtoKit"}],"color":{"standardColorIdentifier":"blue"},"roleHeading":"Article","images":[{"type":"icon","identifier":"bluesky_logo.png"}],"role":"article"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ATProtoKit\/documentation\/ATProtoKit"]]},"references":{"doc://ATProtoKit/documentation/ATProtoKit/ATProtoBluesky":{"role":"symbol","title":"ATProtoBluesky","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The base class that handles all direct Bluesky-related functionality of the ATProtoKit"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"API library.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ATProtoBluesky"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/ATProtoKit\/documentation\/ATProtoKit\/ATProtoBluesky","url":"\/documentation\/atprotokit\/atprotobluesky","type":"topic","fra